    "diagramPlacement": "beside-prompt",
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\overrightarrow{PR}=4(\\underset{\\sim}{a}-\\underset{\\sim}{b})$, so the vectors are parallel.",
      "worked": "By the triangle law,\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{PR}&=\\overrightarrow{PQ}+\\overrightarrow{QR}\\\\&=(6\\underset{\\sim}{a}+\\underset{\\sim}{b})+(-2\\underset{\\sim}{a}-5\\underset{\\sim}{b})\\\\&=4\\underset{\\sim}{a}-4\\underset{\\sim}{b}\\\\&=4(\\underset{\\sim}{a}-\\underset{\\sim}{b}).\\end{aligned}$$\nTherefore $\\overrightarrow{PR}$ is parallel to $\\underset{\\sim}{a}-\\underset{\\sim}{b}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
